WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:08.160
how do share owners keep&nbsp;
abreast of their own companies&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:15.920
what information goes into a firm's annual&nbsp;
report who put out this financial statement&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:22.720
meet one of the 12 and a half million owners&nbsp;
of american industry who risk their savings&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:28.800
in hope of financial reward from the industrial&nbsp;
enterprise that has made america prosperous how do&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:34.320
investors like this know what their companies are&nbsp;
doing they're kept informed by such things as the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:41.280
annual report containing a balance sheet income&nbsp;
statement and generally a great deal more take for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:46.480
example this report by a company that pioneered&nbsp;
in the manufacture of safety razors and blades

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:56.960
the costly automatic machines which today mass&nbsp;
produced blades by the billions every year&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.960 --> 00:01:00.960
are dramatic evidence of what the annual&nbsp;
report means when it tells of assets&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.520 --> 00:01:06.880
behind them as earlier reports would show&nbsp;
stands a record of growth almost as rapid&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:11.760
as the tempo of the machines themselves&nbsp;
these assets descended from a man with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:16.960
an idea for a different way to shave they&nbsp;
were made possible by his efforts and by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.960 --> 00:01:22.480
the capital the public was willing to risk&nbsp;
on his venture continuously reinvesting part&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.480 --> 00:01:27.600
of the earnings to create new assets new&nbsp;
wealth for workers and share owners alike

00:01:31.360 --> 00:01:37.360
the pages of the annual report also show how&nbsp;
companies often diversify as they grow this one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.360 --> 00:01:43.440
added not only new shaving products but pens as&nbsp;
well acquiring this leading manufacturer of ball&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:49.120
point writing instruments by paying 15 million&nbsp;
dollars at the time management decided to add&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.120 --> 00:01:54.480
this venture to earlier successes the reasons&nbsp;
were spelled out carefully for the share owners&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:58.560
who might have instigated some changes of&nbsp;
their own had there been major disagreement&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:04.960
but the acquisition was well made and&nbsp;
well-timed as succeeding reports recorded much&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.960 --> 00:02:09.840
of the investment being recovered through added&nbsp;
profits from the pens in only a few short years

00:02:15.920 --> 00:02:21.120
as the additions of new products and new divisions&nbsp;
are reported the owners find their opportunities&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:26.480
further multiplied their investment has grown&nbsp;
large enough to take them into the manufacture&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.480 --> 00:02:31.840
distribution and sale of feminine beauty&nbsp;
preparations this phase started with purchase&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.840 --> 00:02:38.000
of a company making home permanent wave kits and&nbsp;
it led very quickly to further diversification&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:42.160
and the addition of new employees as&nbsp;
management complemented the various&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.160 --> 00:02:48.480
waving products with shampoos spray nets and&nbsp;
a complete line of hair styling accessories&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:54.240
thus payment for the acquisition was just the&nbsp;
beginning now this firm like others plows back&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.240 --> 00:03:06.320
newly gained profits to meet new competition to&nbsp;
ensure continued growth by the time these scenes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.320 --> 00:03:11.360
were filmed the parent company was little more&nbsp;
than 50 years old in this short lifetime it had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.360 --> 00:03:16.720
quickly outgrown the tiny machine shop where it&nbsp;
was born from larger quarters it took its products&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.720 --> 00:03:22.080
and new facilities to produce them overseas and&nbsp;
around the world before adding the newer items&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.080 --> 00:03:27.440
like these items that have helped produce net&nbsp;
annual sales of more than 200 million dollars&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.080 --> 00:03:32.400
for most of the thousands of owners whose&nbsp;
capital made this achievement possible it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:38.320
would be impractical to visit personally even as&nbsp;
much of their property as our cameramen have seen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.320 --> 00:03:44.480
so widespread and vast is it today but in the&nbsp;
pages of their annual reports they receive a full&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.480 --> 00:03:49.680
accounting keeping up to date not only on today's&nbsp;
events but on the future too as it develops in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.680 --> 00:03:55.280
their company's modern research laboratories here&nbsp;
scores of scientific and technical experts are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.280 --> 00:04:00.880
employed to find ways to improve all products&nbsp;
and production methods and to find brand new&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.880 --> 00:04:07.040
products as well again plow back up profits&nbsp;
is required to back the researchers new ideas&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.040 --> 00:04:11.840
and to pay for the plants and equipment that will&nbsp;
produce them for the market will every project pay&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.840 --> 00:04:19.280
off not by a long shot progress isn't easy it's a&nbsp;
risky business in fact but without it prosperity&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.280 --> 00:04:24.800
would soon wither without continuing investment&nbsp;
in research the march of progress would come to a

00:04:24.800 --> 00:04:27.840
halt

00:04:35.600 --> 00:04:41.840
this project involves new inks for ball point pins

00:04:44.160 --> 00:04:49.120
and here in a room where temperature and&nbsp;
humidity are carefully and constantly controlled&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.120 --> 00:04:52.400
we see one of many tests on fibers and fabrics&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.400 --> 00:04:56.800
what do stockholders think when the reports&nbsp;
show how costly such research work can be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.680 --> 00:05:02.320
by and large they approve wholeheartedly&nbsp;
with many investors actually preferring&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.320 --> 00:05:07.840
to own shares in companies that are aggressively&nbsp;
research-minded feeling confident that companies&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.840 --> 00:05:12.560
spending a good part of their earnings on research&nbsp;
will ultimately return a profit on the investment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.120 --> 00:05:18.240
in research the tools in use sometimes seem as&nbsp;
advanced as the improvements they help achieve&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.240 --> 00:05:22.800
here radioactivity measures the detergent&nbsp;
remaining in a sample of hair after washing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:23.360 --> 00:05:27.920
another project that costs money today but&nbsp;
tomorrow may turn up on the profit side of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:27.920 --> 00:05:37.840
the annual report a document that makes public&nbsp;
regularly the workings of industry the public owns

00:05:40.640 --> 00:05:44.560
now let's see how the report itself is&nbsp;
assembled beginning with a conference that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.560 --> 00:05:48.160
in all probability will bring together&nbsp;
top executives of the company involved&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.720 --> 00:05:52.160
and artists writers and production&nbsp;
men who are expert at the job&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:52.160 --> 00:05:57.120
of presenting a complex array of facts in&nbsp;
simple attractive and easy to understand form&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:57.920 --> 00:06:02.800
everyone works under the pressure of a firm&nbsp;
deadline when annual reports are being assembled&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.800 --> 00:06:07.040
for the finished printing job must be in&nbsp;
the hands of the share owners within three&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.040 --> 00:06:19.840
months of the close of the fiscal year and&nbsp;
at least 15 days before the annual meeting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.880 --> 00:06:26.480
among the earliest steps is the selection of&nbsp;
photographs now used in a majority of reports&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.480 --> 00:06:31.600
they will probably be pictures of the firm's&nbsp;
plants and offices an oil company will want to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:31.600 --> 00:06:36.320
include shots of its refineries the pictures&nbsp;
make the finished report more attractive and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:36.320 --> 00:06:41.600
they also sum up graphically a story that&nbsp;
otherwise could not be so effectively told&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:42.160 --> 00:06:47.840
a firm that makes parts for nuclear submarines&nbsp;
may use a photograph to emphasize that point

00:06:53.840 --> 00:07:01.840
so the work proceeds with layout artists getting&nbsp;
a start even before the final figures are in

00:07:04.800 --> 00:07:09.840
and through it all the figures themselves are&nbsp;
taking shape often with the help of electronic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:09.840 --> 00:07:16.000
computers which make fast work of the inventories&nbsp;
cash on hand sales earnings per share and the like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:16.000 --> 00:07:21.040
the figures are the heart of the annual report&nbsp;
as rapidly as they're compiled and checked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:21.040 --> 00:07:25.440
they're passed along to the production workers&nbsp;
who already know exactly where they should go&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:25.440 --> 00:07:31.680
on exactly what page the system is much the same&nbsp;
as that used in the production of a magazine with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:31.680 --> 00:07:36.320
dummies or mock-ups of the various pages&nbsp;
helping the staff keep track of the

00:07:36.320 --> 00:07:43.840
progress

00:07:47.200 --> 00:07:50.320
a final conference is called&nbsp;
to make last-minute changes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:50.320 --> 00:07:57.840
to check on accuracy and to approve&nbsp;
the booklet or brochure for printing

00:08:00.080 --> 00:08:04.080
now the type is locked in place&nbsp;
or the offset master's completed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:04.080 --> 00:08:07.920
and the presses take over the work the&nbsp;
number of copies they turn out depending&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:07.920 --> 00:08:13.120
basically on the number of people who share&nbsp;
ownership of a particular company for some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:13.120 --> 00:08:17.680
this means a few thousand for others&nbsp;
it may mean a million copies and more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:23.840 --> 00:08:27.840
there must be at least one copy for&nbsp;
every owner whether his interest is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:27.840 --> 00:08:31.360
as little as one share or as&nbsp;
large as hundreds of thousands&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:36.240 --> 00:08:41.280
for annual reports the circulation usually is&nbsp;
larger than the list of stockholders including&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:41.280 --> 00:08:46.800
many others employees customers dealers&nbsp;
the financial community civic leaders and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:46.800 --> 00:08:53.200
newsmen corporations distribute an average of&nbsp;
49 000 reports beyond the number required for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:53.200 --> 00:08:59.600
share owners such wide distribution of so much&nbsp;
information is unique in america only in this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:59.600 --> 00:09:04.880
country is full disclosure of facts about publicly&nbsp;
owned corporations a matter of routine policy

00:09:07.040 --> 00:09:11.280
one of the addresses that frequently turns up&nbsp;
on the mailing list is that of the committee&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:11.280 --> 00:09:17.840
the judge's annual reports in a contest conducted&nbsp;
by financial world magazine its prizes have been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:17.840 --> 00:09:22.640
called the oscars of industry at the head of&nbsp;
the table financial public relations council&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:22.640 --> 00:09:29.120
weston smith originated the idea which involves&nbsp;
initially a large-scale screening that brings&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:29.120 --> 00:09:34.240
the number of entries down to manageable size&nbsp;
for the experts who make the final decisions&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:34.240 --> 00:09:39.520
the contest is credited with inspiring growing&nbsp;
awareness of the importance of annual reports&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:39.520 --> 00:09:44.320
in which the judges looked especially for&nbsp;
comprehensive coverage of essential figures&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:44.320 --> 00:09:49.600
for easy readability and for eye appeal&nbsp;
to mention just a few of the criteria&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:49.600 --> 00:09:54.960
in years gone by annual reports were much&nbsp;
smaller much less informative than they are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:54.960 --> 00:10:06.480
today often a small card was all there was to&nbsp;
a report then they evolved into larger folders

00:10:10.640 --> 00:10:16.400
and this form was the logical end result of&nbsp;
industry's efforts to present full information&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:16.400 --> 00:10:18.720
in an attractive manner easily understood

00:10:22.160 --> 00:10:27.520
sometimes unusual methods are employed&nbsp;
a record company for example has put its&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:27.520 --> 00:10:32.960
president's message on a disc a manufacturer&nbsp;
of gains in educational materials has used&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:32.960 --> 00:10:38.720
a three-dimensional graph that pops up when the&nbsp;
report is opened to attract attention to key facts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:39.280 --> 00:10:45.840
and another report gains share owner interest&nbsp;
by inviting the reader to pull out various tabs

00:10:49.920 --> 00:10:54.640
another unusual method of presentation&nbsp;
involves the use of supplements in sunday&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:54.640 --> 00:10:59.840
newspapers the readership for these&nbsp;
supplements is rated in the millions

00:11:03.040 --> 00:11:08.080
in the continuing campaign to extend knowledge&nbsp;
about their operations to an ever wider&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:08.080 --> 00:11:12.720
audience companies frequently take smaller&nbsp;
advertisements in newspapers and magazines&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:13.600 --> 00:11:19.040
the gist of their annual reports this widespread&nbsp;
dissemination of the facts about american industry&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:19.040 --> 00:11:25.440
may help explain why today one out of every eight&nbsp;
americans own stock in one or more corporations&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:26.000 --> 00:11:30.160
here a few thousand of those individuals&nbsp;
some of the five hundred thousand who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:30.160 --> 00:11:35.040
own stock in one firm gather for their&nbsp;
annual meeting although only a fraction&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:35.040 --> 00:11:41.840
of the company's owners attend the largest&nbsp;
auditorium in town is filled to overflowing

00:11:48.400 --> 00:11:53.440
chief purpose of the gathering is to let the&nbsp;
share owners hear directly from management a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:53.440 --> 00:11:58.720
more detailed account of the year's activities&nbsp;
as described in the annual report that was sent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:58.720 --> 00:12:04.000
out at least two weeks prior to this meeting&nbsp;
after management has talked the stockholders&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:04.000 --> 00:12:08.640
are heard from as they let management know&nbsp;
what they think of the way things are going&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:08.640 --> 00:12:14.960
for these men and women all just average citizens&nbsp;
are the real owners of american industry the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:14.960 --> 00:12:20.800
capitalists constantly under attack in some areas&nbsp;
of the world but vocal expression is only one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:20.800 --> 00:12:26.160
way the share owner makes his opinion known for&nbsp;
secret ballots on all issues have been sent out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:26.160 --> 00:12:30.400
to each one and now as the meeting&nbsp;
proceeds those ballots are counted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:31.120 --> 00:12:37.840
unlike the phony product peddled from behind the&nbsp;
iron curtain this is a real people's capitalism

